<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The app's only widget.

  ⚠️ **The resize range is load-bearing, not decoration.** The provider ships six `RemoteViews`
  keyed on `SizeF` — four row forms (120×90, 180×165, 250×275, 300×385), the compact board (300×420)
  and the full board (300×680) — and the HOST picks between them. A range that never reaches a
  breakpoint means that variant can never be drawn, however carefully it was built, and nothing
  would report it: the widget would simply look like it had one layout. So the floor here is exactly
  the smallest breakpoint, and the ceiling is well past the largest.

  ⚠️ The ceiling is 1000dp, not the 640 it was, because the full board now GROWS: its agenda list
  takes every dp above 680 at any height. The owner's widget is placed around 830dp tall; at 640 a
  strict launcher would clamp it, and the list is the thing the extra height is for.

  `targetCellWidth`/`targetCellHeight` are the size it is PLACED at (API 31+, and minSdk is 31 so
  there is no legacy fallback to keep in step). Four by three lands a fresh placement around the third
  variant — rich enough to be worth having on sight, with room left to grow, which is the behaviour
  the resize range exists to reward.

  `widgetCategory` keeps `keyguard`. ⚠️ Whether that does anything on this device is genuinely open:
  the platform dropped lock-screen widgets in 5.0 and reintroduced them in 15 QPR1+, and launchers
  differ. It costs nothing where it is ignored.

  `previewLayout` is the real layout rather than a bitmap, so the picker renders the actual thing.
  It shows empty rows there — the picker has no data — which is why `description` carries the pitch.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:description="@string/widget_lock_description"
    android:minWidth="180dp"
    android:minHeight="110dp"
    android:minResizeWidth="120dp"
    android:minResizeHeight="90dp"
    android:maxResizeWidth="500dp"
    android:maxResizeHeight="1000dp"
    android:targetCellWidth="4"
    android:targetCellHeight="3"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="1800000"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/widget_lock"
    android:previewLayout="@layout/widget_lock"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen|keyguard" />
